<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</h1><p class="st-meta">1816 CE – 1861 CE · capital Naples</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The largest pre-unification Italian state, the Bourbon kingdom of Naples and Sicily, overthrown by Garibaldi's Thousand in 1860.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> restored him, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-the-two-sicilies">Ferdinand IV of Naples</a> and III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> merged the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-naples">Kingdom of Naples</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sicilian-kingdom-of-1848">Kingdom of Sicily</a> in December 1816, becoming Ferdinand I of the Two Sicilies, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom was an absolute monarchy that put down revolts in 1820 and 1848; Sicilians resented losing their autonomy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-the-two-sicilies">Ferdinand II</a> opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy's</a> first railway, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portici">Portici</a>, in 1839 and built a strong navy, but his harsh repression earned him the nickname King Bomba. The south remained largely rural, with powerful landowners and widespread poverty.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1860 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/expedition-of-the-thousand">Expedition of the Thousand</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> held out at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaeta">Gaeta</a> until February 1861, and the kingdom was annexed to the new <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies.jpg" alt="Kingdom of the Two Sicilies" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Flopao; derivative work by ZuppaDiCarlo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_the_Two_Sicilies_(1816)_(Sodacan_style).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1816 CE – 1861 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Naples</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ferdinand I of the Two Sicilies, Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies, Francis II of the Two Sicilies</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Neapolitan, Sicilian, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Two Sicilies, Regno delle Due Sicilie</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies" aria-label="Kingdom of the Two Sicilies on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5029 720 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of the Two Sicilies lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5349 976L5333 1064M5349 976L5349 976M5349 976L5226 1028M5349 976L5304 942M5349 976L5333 1064"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5333 1064h0M5349 976h0M5226 1028h0M5304 942h0M5333 1064h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5349 976h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5349 976h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Naples. <a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
